g cash advantage over Collins. Markets and most raters put this near Safe D, but Georgia's narrow partisan lean and residual midterm uncertainty justify stopping at Likely D.", "watch": "A late tightening toward the governor's race environment, or Collins closing the fundraising gap with outside spending, could narrow the margin.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Jon Ossoff (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Senator Jon Ossoff seeks a second term against Representative Mike Collins in a state that leans slightly Republican but has favored Democrats in recent statewide races. Polling throughout the fall has been remarkably consistent, with Ossoff leading by seven to twelve points in surveys from both independent and Republican-affiliated pollsters, including a late October University of Georgia poll showing a eight-point edge.\n\nThe resource picture is lopsided: Ossoff has raised over $115 million and holds $15 million on hand, while Collins has about $1 million. Prediction markets price Ossoff's chances around 96 percent, and most expert ratings land at Likely D, with a few calling it Safe or Solid Democratic. The main question is the size of the win, not the winner.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9499, "margin": 8.78}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9449, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9229, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9348, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9317, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9355, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9397, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9457, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9522, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9495, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9478, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9479, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9545, "margin": 8.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.928, "margin": 8.5}, {"date